meta {
  name: Run billing (ops)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/ops/billing/run?asOf={{firstDueDate}}&contractId={{contractId}}
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  asOf: {{firstDueDate}}
  contractId: {{contractId}}
}

headers {
  Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{opsToken}}
}

docs {
  Ops or admin. Runs the billing cycle as of a day (default today) and sends what is due to the simulated payment provider. `asOf` is the first due date from "Get schedule", so the first instalment is charged now; a future day is accepted only where `BILLING_FUTURE_RUNS_ENABLED` is on (the default outside production). Without `contractId` it bills every contract.

  The provider collects and calls back within seconds; then "List charges" shows the instalment as `paid`. An amount ending in 13 cents is refused for insufficient funds; one ending in 14 cents is collected and then returned by the bank (`MD06`) a few seconds later, so the charge is `failed` again and the statement shows a `return` line; dunning's retry is then collected.
}
